## Exact source-surface rule

For `ok`, return the shortest exact source phrase that completely names the
selected unit or metric. Do not add words such as `number of`, `content`,
`cytosolic`, a parenthetical abbreviation, or a scale explanation unless those
words are part of the source phrase tied to the selected value. Do not reorder
words, expand abbreviations, or replace punctuation. When `unit_text` is
nonempty, copy it verbatim. If an exact complete source span cannot be selected,
use `unsure` rather than a scientifically similar paraphrase.
